    "blind_spots": [
      "actix `configure`: the routes a function registers on a `ServiceConfig` keep the path they are written with, because the function is not followed to the scope that applies it",
      "routers passed as values the connector cannot follow: a router built in another crate, re-exported with `pub use`, kept in a field, handed over as an argument, returned from a branch or mounted with `nest_service` is not placed under the prefix it is mounted at",
      "router mounts are followed only to a limit: routers nested more than 64 deep, or entered more than 50000 times in the walk from one router that nothing mounts, are not followed past it, and the routes below the cut keep the paths they are written with",
      "mounts written `Type::router()`: only `Self::name`, a function of the file and a path to a function of a module are followed, so the routes of a router built by an associated function of a type keep the paths they are written with",
      "names that a glob import brings in, such as `prop` after `use proptest::prelude::*`, are not known: a path that starts with one is reported as an unknown package",
      "a crate target with more than 10000 modules is read up to that many, and a path into the modules past the cut is not found",
      "a module declared twice under different `cfg`s, such as `unix.rs` and `win.rs` behind one `mod sys;`, is the first declaration to every path that names it: the other file resolves its own `crate::`, `self::` and `super::` paths, and no path reaches it by name",
      "paths written inside `macro_rules!` bodies are not read",
      "items generated by macros, such as modules and routes, and code included with `include!` from generated files are not read"
    ]
